\viewkind4\uc1\pard\sa160\sl252\slmult1\i\f0\fs22 Library Manager Cassandra Sargent \kerning2 provided an update on the Summer Discovery Program. Participants of all ages can earn a free book and prize for every six books read or activities completed. She highlighted that the library is offering a wide range of programs this summer\kerning0  \kerning2 including music, performers, and adult events\kerning0 .\line\line Waste Management Recycling Education Representative Bobby Bell \kerning2 provided reminders that there will be no break in service on \kerning0 June 19, 2026 (\kerning2 Juneteenth\kerning0 )\kerning2 . \kerning0 He also\kerning2  announced that the City\rquote s second paper-shredding event of the year will take place at Mira Costa High School \kerning0 on Saturday, June 20, 2026, \kerning2 from 9\kerning0 :00 AM \kerning2 -11\kerning0 :00 AM\kerning2 . Residents and business owners may bring up to three banker boxes for secure paper recycling.\highlight1\kerning0\line\line\highlight0 Planning Manager Adam Finestone \kerning2 reported that two Project Pulse design workshops were held, with more than 70 community members providing input on concepts for Parking Lot 3 and 400 Manhattan Beach Boulevard. The feedback will guide the City\rquote s design consultant in preparing conceptual designs, which will be presented at a public open house\kerning0  at the Joslyn Community Center\kerning2  on Wednesday, July 15,\kerning0  2026,\kerning2  from 6\kerning0 :00 PM\kerning2  to 8\kerning0 :00 PM\kerning2 .\kerning0  \kerning2 This will be the final opportunity for community input before the designs go to City Council later this summer.\kerning0\line\line\pard Cultural Arts Supervisor Eric Brinkman \kerning2 announced details for the City\rquote s Juneteenth celebration \kerning0 at Polliwog Park \kerning2 on Sunday, June 21, from 2\kerning0 :00 PM\kerning2  to 7\kerning0 :00 PM\kerning2 . The event will feature live music, cultural performances, food vendors, community organizations, family activities, and educational programming. Los Angeles County Supervisor Holly Mitchell will attend, \kerning0 and \kerning2 Dr. Anthony Lee will provide a presentation on the history of Bruce\rquote s Beach and introduce artist April Banks.\kerning0  \cf2\i0\f1\fs24\par
